///1SIZE

SIZE.CMD
by K. Maeda.  Originally written 1-3-83.  Revised 10-16-84.
Public Domain Software - JUG-CP/M

SIZE looks at the header record of an executable file, and reports the
base address and minimum size of the various segments within the file:
code, data, extra and stack segments.


///2USAGE
SIZE may be invoked in one of two ways:

    SIZE filename.ext <ENTER>  or
    SIZE <ENTER>

If a filename is entered as a command line argument, SIZE will report
its findings about that file to the screen, and then exit.

If SIZE is invoked with no command line argument, it enters interactive
mode, and prompts you to enter a filename.  After reporting on the file
name you enter, SIZE will prompt you to enter another filename.  This
can be handy when you want to examine more than one file at a single
session.
